Project Axiom - Initial Polish & Architectural Upgrade:
  # Comprehensive roadmap to replace synthetic sinusoidal embeddings with a learnable VRAM embedding matrix,
  # eliminate the billion-ID partition memory wall, unify text/number namespaces, and cure optimizer amnesia.

  Phase 1: Ingestion & Modality Unification (Data Layer)
    ✔ 1.1 Unify Text & Number Namespaces @done @parser @architecture
      - Remove data_num and user_numbers separation in parser.hpp
      - Ingest numbers directly as textual tokens (e.g. "9.8" or "9", ".", "8")
      - Preserve semantic co-occurrence between words and numerical quantities (e.g. "gravity" and "9.8")
    ✔ 1.2 Sanitize Document Ingestion & Eliminate PDF Byte Streaming @done @parser @data
      - Stop treating .pdf, .docx, and formatted text documents as raw binary byte streams in bulk_tokenize_directory
      - Eliminate zlib/FlateDecode compressed entropy ingestion
      - Pass document files through a text/equation extraction pre-pass so terms like "mass" and "acceleration" enter as linguistic tokens
    ✔ 1.3 Restrict Raw Byte Tokenization to Genuine Binary Assets @done @parser @multimodal
      - Route only genuine visual media (PNG, JPG, BMP) and audio waveforms (WAV, OGG) to byte-level discrete tokenizers

  Phase 2: Dense Contiguous Early-Fusion Indexing (Tokenizer Layer)
    ✔ 2.1 Eradicate Billion-Scale Modality Offsets @done @tokenizer @memory
      - Delete 1,000,000,000 (numbers), 2,000,000,000 (images), 3,000,000,000 (video), and 4,000,000,000 (voice) base ID offsets in parser.hpp
      - Prevent multi-gigabyte VRAM allocation crashes caused by indexing sparse multi-billion ID tables
    ✔ 2.2 Establish Fixed Bounded Vocabulary (V = 65,536) @done @tokenizer @vram
      - Cap vocabulary to a dense 16-bit addressable range [0, 65535]
      - Guarantee fixed ~4.19 MB VRAM footprint for bf16 embedding table
    ✔ 2.3 Partition Contiguous Modality ID Blocks @done @tokenizer @architecture
      - Slots [0 .. 3]: Special reserved tokens (<PAD>=0, <UNK>=1, <BOS>=2, <EOS>=3)
      - Slots [4 .. 64,511]: Text words, subwords, numbers, and mathematical symbols
      - Slots [64,512 .. 64,767]: Discrete visual bytes (256 slots for 0x00..0xFF)
      - Slots [64,768 .. 65,023]: Discrete acoustic bytes (256 slots for 0x00..0xFF)
      - Slots [65,024 .. 65,535]: Reserved expansion slots for future modality codebooks

  Phase 3: VRAM Embedding Matrix & Memory Allocation (GPU State)
    ✔ 3.1 Define GpuEmbeddings Structure in gpu_types.cuh @done @cuda @types
      - Declare d_table (__nv_bfloat16*) for fast coalesced Tensor Core / gather reads
      - Declare d_table_master (float*) for high-precision FP32 gradient accumulation
      - Track vocab_size (65,536) and embedding_dim (32)
    ✔ 3.2 Implement Allocation & Chaos Initialization in memory_allocation.cu @done @cuda @memory
      - Allocate d_table (65,536 * 32 * sizeof(__nv_bfloat16) = 4,194,304 bytes)
      - Allocate d_table_master (65,536 * 32 * sizeof(float) = 8,388,608 bytes)
      - Initialize table with uniform chaos in [-1/sqrt(D), +1/sqrt(D)] (approx [-0.176, +0.176] for D=32)
    ✔ 3.3 Implement Systematic Teardown in free_gpu() @done @cuda @memory
      - Ensure cudaFree releases d_table and d_table_master on shutdown to prevent VRAM memory leaks

  Phase 4: Forward Gather Kernel & PCIe Bandwidth Optimization (Compute Layer)
    ✔ 4.1 Invert Host-to-Device Dataflow @done @pcie @bandwidth
      - Stop CPU-side float vector generation in Parser::embedding (retire embedded_data.bin disk/RAM buffer)
      - Upload only 128 uint32_t token IDs across PCIe per context window (512 bytes vs 8,192 bytes of floats)
    ✔ 4.2 Write Branchless Gather CUDA Kernel in forward_pass.cu @done @cuda @kernel
      - Implement gather_embeddings_kernel<<<grid, block, 0, stream>>>
      - Each thread maps directly to (token_idx, dim_idx) and loads d_table[token_id * 32 + d] into d_context_window
      - Zero warp divergence across multimodal tokens; 100% coalesced global memory reads
    ✔ 4.3 Synchronize with CUTLASS EVT GEMM @done @cuda @kernel
      - Ensure gather kernel writes to d_context_window prior to Tensor Core matrix multiplication

  Phase 5: Backward Scatter Kernel & Semantic Emergence (Learning Layer)
    ✔ 5.1 Calculate Input Gradients (dL/dx) in backward_pass.cu @done @cuda @backprop
      - Compute dL/dx_j = sum_{i=0}^{out_dim-1} dz_i * W_{ij} inside backward pass
      - Pass gradient signal backward through the linear projection layer into the input context window
    ✔ 5.2 Implement Backward Scatter Kernel with atomicAdd @done @cuda @kernel
      - For each context token position j with token ID T_j, accumulate gradient into FP32 master table:
        atomicAdd(&d_table_master[T_j * 32 + d], -learning_rate * dx_{j, d})
      - Eliminate race conditions when common tokens (e.g. "the") appear multiple times in the same context window
    ✔ 5.3 Round Master FP32 to Device bf16 Table @done @cuda @precision
      - Convert d_table_master[T_j * 32 + d] into d_table[T_j * 32 + d] via __float2bfloat16() for subsequent forward steps
      - Physically cluster semantically related tokens (e.g. "bulk" and "training") in 32D hyperspace over time

  Phase 6: Optimizer Evolution & Curing Amnesia (Optimization Layer)
    ✔ 6.1 Allocate Momentum & Variance VRAM Buffers @done @cuda @optimizer
      - Allocate first moment tensor m_t (float*) and second moment tensor v_t (float*) for all parameters
    ✔ 6.2 Implement Fused AdamW Kernel in CUDA @done @cuda @optimizer
      - Update parameters using bias-corrected first and second moments:
        m_t = beta1 * m_{t-1} + (1 - beta1) * g
        v_t = beta2 * v_{t-1} + (1 - beta2) * g^2
        theta = theta - lr * (m_hat / (sqrt(v_hat) + eps) + weight_decay * theta)
      - Provide directional velocity and curvature memory across training steps

  Phase 7: Unified Model Checkpointing (Persistence Layer)
    ✔ 7.1 Extend AxiomWeightHeader in ai.hpp @done @persistence @io
      - Add vocab_size (uint64_t) and embedding_dim (uint64_t) to binary header
      - Validate header magic 'AXIOM_V1' and exact byte layout
    ✔ 7.2 Persist Master Embedding Table in AI::save_weights / load_weights @done @persistence @io
      - Serialize d_table_master alongside weights and biases into weights.axiom
      - Restore learned semantic coordinates and upload to GPU VRAM on engine startup
